/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Start from the fundamental relation for a closed system of C components: dG = −S dT + V dP + Σ μi dni.
   - μi is chemical potential in J/mol; μi° is the standard chemical potential in J/mol; R = 8.314 J mol⁻¹ K⁻¹; T is temperature in K; fi is fugacity in Pa; fi° is the standard fugacity in Pa.
   - The fugacity form is the working criterion.
   - At fixed T and P, a stable phase has the lowest G.
   - Use the criteria in order.
*/
